							"role": "user",
							"content": [
								{
									"text": "You are a recruiter about to have an intake meeting with the hiring manager for this role, to pressure-test this JD before you start sourcing. Below is the full JD (raw Notion block JSON — extract the text from the rich_text / plain_text fields):\n{{23.json}}\n\nGenerate CHALLENGING questions YOU (the recruiter) will ask the HIRING MANAGER — these are NOT candidate screening questions and NOT questions to ask a candidate. Actively look for inconsistencies in the JD and make the hiring manager defend or clarify them: does the job title actually match the stated mission/scope? Does the tech stack match what this person will really be doing day to day? Do the listed responsibilities match the seniority implied by the title? Is anything vague, contradictory, or overstated between the title, the mission, the stack, and the day-to-day tasks? These REPLACE the generic 'pick a bucket' profile-specific questions (Tech roles / Product / Revenue / Marketing / Customer Enablement) in the standard intake template, so every question must be grounded in something ACTUALLY written in THIS JD, not generic.\n\nHard rules on what to avoid — these questions must NEVER resemble or overlap with the standard intake template's own questions:\n- Do not ask about team vibe, how the team makes decisions, why the role exists, first-30-days expectations, a typical week, what's already built vs a blank page, must-haves vs nice-to-haves, the interview process, the panel, sourcing, or closing — the template already covers those.\n- Never ask what success looks like or how success will be measured, in any form, at any time horizon.\n- If a question could apply to any role rather than this specific JD's actual wording, it is wrong — rewrite it to cite something specific from the JD.\n\nOutput format is STRICT and MANDATORY, no exceptions even if the JD text looks incomplete or malformed — work with whatever JD content you have, never comment on its completeness:\n- Output EXACTLY 7 lines, nothing before line 1 and nothing after line 7\n- NO preamble, NO introduction, NO commentary, NO blank lines between values\n- The very first character of your output must be the first character of question 1\n\nLine 1: [must-ask challenge question 1]\nLine 2: [must-ask challenge question 2]\nLine 3: [must-ask challenge question 3]\nLine 4: [must-ask challenge question 4]\nLine 5: [must-ask challenge question 5]\nLine 6: [ask-if-relevant challenge question 1 — only include a real question if the JD genuinely warrants it; otherwise write None]\nLine 7: [ask-if-relevant challenge question 2 — same rule, or None if only one applies]\n\nRules:\n- Each question max 30 words\n- Phrase every question as something the RECRUITER asks the HIRING MANAGER — never a question addressed to a candidate\n- NO double quotes anywhere in the output\n- NO backslashes anywhere in the output\n- Each value on a single line, no line breaks within a value",
									"type": "text"
								}
							],
							"inputType": "multiple"
						}
					],
					"max_tokens": 600,
					"temperature": 0
				},
